The project's common/ directory is on the compiler include path, so its
endian.h shadows the libc <endian.h> for any system header that includes
it. uClibc's bits/waitstatus.h does exactly that, finds the project header
instead, never gets __BYTE_ORDER defined, and compiles both endian branches
of its bitfields. Rename the internal header to a name that cannot collide.

diff --git a/common/endian.h b/common/faac_endian.h
similarity index 100%
rename from common/endian.h
rename to common/faac_endian.h
